    "title": "New apartment complex to add more living options in Abilene - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Lauren Dossey ,\n9 hours ago A new apartment complex is set to bring more housing options to Abilene as developers look to meet the city's growing demand for residential space.\nHighland Meadows Apartment Homes, a new development planned at 2108 Scottish Road, has completed its review with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation.\nOnce complete, the project will add 241 apartment units to Abilene's housing market.\nAccording to the complex's filing with TDLR, the apartment community will include a three-story corridor-style building with an integrated clubhouse, eight three-story garden-style residential buildings, four garage structures, nine carports and a cabana.\nThe estimated project cost is listed as $500,000, covering 5,453 square feet of facility space, according to TDLR.\nAccording to TDLR records, construction on the complex began March 15 and is expected to be completed by Sept. 15, 2028.\nThis article originally appeared on Abilene Reporter-News: New apartment complex to add more living options in Abilene",
    "summary": "9 hours ago A new apartment complex is set to bring more housing options to Abilene as developers look to meet the city's growing demand for residential space. Highland Meadows Apartment Homes, a new development planned at 2108 Scottish Road, has completed its review with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation. Once complete, the project will add 241 apartment units to Abilene's housing market. The estimated project cost is listed as $500,000, covering 5,453 square feet of facility space, according to TDLR.",
